    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d151">

                <pb facs="0167" n="155" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg155"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00/1157: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Helsinki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-04-25T16:00:00+02:00">April 25, 1939—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 25—1:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>62. Your telegram No. 29 and my No. 59.<anchor n="39" xml:id="d151-f1"/> In
                    response to my inquiry today Minister of Foreign Affairs told me that Finnish
                    Government looked upon the President’s message as important contribution to
                    peace in that the head of a powerful nation should at this time hold out an
                    offer of negotiation for settlement of pending differences. He said that he had
                    reports from Stockholm and Copenhagen that this was also the view of the
                    Governments there but he had no report from Oslo. He added that according to
                    information Hitler’s forthcoming speech in response to the President’s message
                    would be “very strong” but would not close the door to further discussion since
                    it was becoming more evident that British patience was coming rapidly to an end
                    and that public opinion in Britain might force the Government to drastic action
                    which he did not define.</p>
                <p>I did not bring up the suggestion that Finnish Government might issue a public
                    statement along the lines of your telegram No. 29 and elicited the foregoing by
                    what I said was a personal inquiry.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
